      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T19:14:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we add parameters that let the client specify the outset? We\u0027ve previously talked about more complicated things (having extra SkSL that defines how the image filter participates in geometry), but it seems like we could do something simpler at the C++ side when you make the instance. I was going to suggest an output limit, too - but I guess you can do that by just wrapping the filter in a CropFilter? Regardless, having a sample-radius parameter (or similar) would be straightforward?",
      "parentUuid": "bc485e45_84081158",
      "revId": "7708e5bd3c3e6793c9ee9d4903d9cb7882c1f25e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
